To configure a Nokia router to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes from EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
            send-to-ebgp ipv6
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration:
1. Enables adding link-bandwidth extended communities to received IPv6 routes from EBGP peers (`add-to-received-ebgp`)
2. Allows sending these link-bandwidth extended communities in IPv6 routes advertised to EBGP peers (`send-to-ebgp`)
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
