To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes from EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type ebgp
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
            send-to-ebgp ipv6
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This configuration:
1. Creates an EBGP group
2. Enables link-bandwidth functionality
3. Configures the router to:
   - Add link-bandwidth extended communities to received IPv6 routes from directly connected EBGP peers (`add-to-received-ebgp`)
   - Allow sending of link-bandwidth extended communities in IPv6 routes to EBGP peers (`send-to-ebgp`)
------------
