## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to automatically attach link-bandwidth extended communities to all received unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> link-bandwidth add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group. This command ensures that the link-bandwidth extended community is added to unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers.
