To configure a Nokia router to allow BGP to propagate routes that are not the best path in the routing table, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        always-compare-med zero
        deterministic-med
        ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv4 ipv6
    exit
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable MED comparison for routes from different AS neighbors (`always-compare-med zero`)
2. Ensure deterministic MED comparison across route updates (`deterministic-med`)
3. Treat EBGP and IBGP routes equally during path selection (`ebgp-ibgp-equal`)

This configuration allows BGP to consider and potentially propagate alternative paths beyond just the single best path.
