To configure a Nokia router to advertise VPN IPv4 routes over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 next-hop address, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4
        neighbor <ipv6-neighbor-address>
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            local-address <local-ipv6-address>
exit all
```

Key points:
- `extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4` enables the capability to advertise VPN-IPv4 routes with IPv6 next-hops
- The neighbor configuration uses IPv6 addresses for both the peer and local-address
- The VPN-IPv4 address family must be enabled in the BGP group

This configuration allows the router to:
1. Establish BGP sessions over IPv6 transport
2. Advertise VPN-IPv4 routes
3. Use IPv6 addresses as next-hops for these VPN routes
