To configure a Nokia router to allow active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to be advertised to a BGP peer with an RFC 3107 label, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
    advertise-inactive
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable the advertising of inactive BGP routes (`advertise-inactive`), allowing the /32 LDP FEC prefixes to be advertised even if they are not the most preferred route.
2. Configure BGP to advertise the capability to receive labeled IPv4 routes (`extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4`), which is required for RFC 3107 label support.

Apply these commands under the relevant BGP neighbor or group context if the configuration needs to be specific to a particular peer.
