To configure Nokia routers to allow LLGR stale routes to be advertised to all peers, including those that can exit AS 65530, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    advertise-inactive
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
        restart-time 300
    exit
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable the advertising of inactive BGP routes (`advertise-inactive`)
2. Configure graceful restart with notification support (`enable-notification`)
3. Set the graceful restart timer (`restart-time`)

The configuration ensures that stale routes will be advertised during a graceful restart event, including to peers in AS 65530. Apply these at the global BGP level to affect all peers.
