## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables acceptance of link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes (`accept-from-ebgp ipv4`)
2. Allows sending these link-bandwidth values when readvertising IPv4 routes with next-hop-self (`send-to-ebgp ipv4`)

The settings must be configured under the specific BGP group where the EBGP peers are defined.
