To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration will:
1. Enable acceptance of link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
2. Allow sending of link-bandwidth extended communities to EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
3. Ensure proper next-hop-self behavior when readvertising routes

For optimal operation, ensure the BGP session is properly established and that the remote peer also supports link-bandwidth extended communities.
