To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    aigp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            aigp
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the IP address of the BGP neighbor where you want to enable AIGP support. This configuration enables the Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute, allowing BGP to consider end-to-end IGP metrics across multiple autonomous systems during path selection.
