Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        ldp rsvp-te sr-te
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration enables BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes by specifying the tunnel types (LDP, RSVP-TE, and SR-TE) that can be used for next-hop resolution of these routes.
