## Proposed answer:
To tie BGP neighbor session state with BFD session status on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            bfd-enable
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will enable BFD for the specific BGP neighbor, causing the BGP session state to follow the BFD session status.

For enabling BFD at the BGP group level (applies to all neighbors in the group):

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        bfd-enable
```
