Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable BFD session monitoring for BGP neighbor connectivity on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            bfd-enable
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will tie the BGP session state to the BFD session state for faster failure detection.

For global BGP BFD enablement (applies to all neighbors):
```cli
configure router bgp
    bfd-enable
exit
```
