Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP) on a Nokia router:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "BMP_STATION_1"
            report-local-routes
            connection
                address 192.0.2.1 port 5000
                no shutdown
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `"BMP_STATION_1"` with your preferred station name, and `192.0.2.1` and `5000` with the actual IP address and port of your BMP monitoring station.

To enable additional BMP-related features in BGP, you can also configure:

```
configure
    router
        bgp
            rapid-withdrawal
            enable-peer-tracking
            best-path-selection
                ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv4 ipv6
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```
