To configure your Nokia router to prefer BGP routes with valid RPKI origin validation states, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        compare-origin-validation-state
        origin-invalid-unusable
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable comparison of RPKI origin validation states during BGP best path selection (preferring Valid > Not-Found > Invalid)
2. Mark routes with Invalid origin validation state as unusable

The configuration ensures routes with Valid RPKI states are preferred while completely excluding Invalid routes from consideration.
