Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to advertise the default BGP route (0.0.0.0/0) to specific peers within an established BGP group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            default-originate
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of the specific peer(s) you want to advertise the default route to. 

If you need to ensure the default route is advertised even if it's not the best path, also include:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        advertise-inactive
