To prevent Nokia routers from using 4-byte Autonomous System Numbers in BGP configuration, configure the `autonomous-system` command with a 2-byte AS number (range 1 to 65535) under the router context:

```
configure router
    autonomous-system <1-65535>
exit
```

Additionally, if you need to ensure compatibility with peers that don't support 4-byte AS numbers, you can use the `local-as` command with a 2-byte AS number in the BGP configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    local-as <1-65535>
exit
``` 

These configurations will restrict the router to using only 2-byte AS numbers in BGP operations.
