To configure a Nokia router to strictly support only IPv4 routing exchanges with BGP peer 192.0.2.1 without negotiating any new capabilities, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group "IPv4_ONLY_GROUP"
            neighbor 192.0.2.1
                peer-as <PEER_AS_NUMBER>
                family ipv4
                no extended-nh-encoding
                no enable-notification
                no advertise-inactive
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<PEER_AS_NUMBER>` with the actual autonomous system number of your BGP peer. This configuration:
- Creates a dedicated BGP group for IPv4-only peering
- Disables extended next-hop encoding capabilities
- Disables notification support
- Prevents advertising inactive routes
- Restricts the session to IPv4 family only
