To prevent BGP peers from negotiating new capabilities while maintaining strict IPv4 routing exchange support on a Nokia router, you need to disable BGP capability negotiation at both the global BGP level and for specific peers/groups. Here are the required CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        no capability-negotiation
        group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
            no capability-negotiation
            family ipv4
            exit
        neighbor "IP_ADDRESS"
            no capability-negotiation
            family ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Key points:
1. `no capability-negotiation` at both global BGP and peer/group levels prevents any new capability negotiations
2. Explicitly configuring `family ipv4` ensures only IPv4 routing exchange is supported
3. Apply these settings to all relevant BGP groups and neighbors

This configuration will maintain basic IPv4 routing exchange while preventing any additional capability negotiations with peers.
------------
