To prevent route reflection to clients within the BGP group "INTERNAL_PEERS" on a Nokia router, remove the route reflector cluster configuration from the group or neighbor level. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "INTERNAL_PEERS"
        no cluster
    exit
exit
```

If the cluster is configured at the global BGP level instead, you would need to reconfigure it to exclude the "INTERNAL_PEERS" group from being treated as route reflector clients. The exact approach depends on your current configuration, but typically you would ensure the group or its neighbors don't have the cluster configuration applied.
