Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To prevent a Nokia router from reflecting BGP routes to all clients within a specific group, you need to configure route reflection with specific clusters or locations. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id>
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name, `<cluster-id>` with a unique cluster identifier (e.g., an IP address), and `<location-id>` with a value between 1-16. This will ensure routes are only reflected to clients in the specified location/group combination.

For example:
```
configure router bgp
    group RR-CLIENTS
        cluster 192.0.2.1 orr-location 5
exit
```
