Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To remove standard and large BGP communities when advertising routes to a specific peer, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-IP> 
no export community
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-IP>` with the specific peer's IP address. This command will remove all BGP communities (both standard and large) from routes advertised to that peer.
