## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to prevent BGP sessions from using fast external failover?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP sessions from using fast external failover on a Nokia router, you need to adjust the BGP timers to increase the hold time and disable rapid withdrawal. Here are the necessary CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    no rapid-withdrawal
    keepalive 60
exit
```

These commands:
1. Disable rapid withdrawal of routes (`no rapid-withdrawal`)
2. Increase the keepalive timer to 60 seconds (default is 30), which will automatically set the hold timer to 180 seconds (3x keepalive)

The increased keepalive/hold timers make the session less sensitive to temporary failures, while disabling rapid withdrawal ensures normal withdrawal behavior rather than immediate route removal.
