## User question:
How to prevent Nokia routers from installing both labeled and unlabeled BGP routes into RTM and FIB while maintaining the BGP session?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent Nokia routers from installing both labeled and unlabeled BGP routes into RTM and FIB while maintaining the BGP session, you need to configure route policies to filter these routes. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp rib-management
    no ipv4
    no label-ipv4
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Disables the installation of unlabeled IPv4 BGP routes into RTM/FIB (`no ipv4`)
2. Disables the installation of labeled IPv4 BGP routes into RTM/FIB (`no label-ipv4`)

The BGP sessions will remain established, but the routes won't be installed in the routing table or forwarding information base.
