How to configure Nokia router to accept a maximum of 1024 dynamic BGP sessions from remote peers within a specific BGP peer group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to accept a maximum of 1024 dynamic BGP sessions from remote peers within a specific BGP peer group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        dynamic-neighbor-limit 1024
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with the name of your BGP peer group. This configuration sets the maximum number of dynamic BGP sessions allowed for the specified peer group to 1024.
