Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as <remote-as-number>
        dynamic-neighbors <interface-name> [max-peers <maximum-peers>]
exit
```

Replace:
- `<group-name>` with your desired peer group name
- `<remote-as-number>` with the remote AS number for the peer group
- `<interface-name>` with the interface where dynamic neighbors will be discovered
- `<maximum-peers>` (optional) with the maximum number of peers allowed on the interface

For example:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type external
        peer-as 65001
        dynamic-neighbors "to-core" max-peers 50
exit
```
