To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        enable-peer-tracking
        no disable-capability-negotiation
        no disable-4byte-asn
exit exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP peer group name. This configuration:
1. Creates the BGP peer group
2. Enables peer tracking for faster convergence
3. Allows capability negotiation by default
4. Permits 4-byte ASN support by default

For additional dynamic session features, you may also consider adding:
```
extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
rapid-withdrawal
``` 

to the group configuration if needed for your specific use case.
