Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure Nokia routers for VPN route exchange between different autonomous systems in a BGP environment, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    autonomous-system <your-local-as>
    router-id <your-router-id>
    rapid-withdrawal
    enable-peer-tracking
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
    group <ebgp-group-name>
        type external
        peer-as <remote-as>
        next-hop-self
        disable-capability-negotiation
        enforce-first-as
        loop-detect ignore-loop
        neighbor <remote-peer-ip>
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

For VPN route leaking between autonomous systems:
```
configure router bgp rib-management vpn-ipv4
    leak-import "<policy-name>"
    exit
```

If you need to enable EIBGP load balancing for VPN routes:
```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    ebgp-ibgp-equal vpn-ipv4
    exit
```

Replace `<your-local-as>`, `<your-router-id>`, `<ebgp-group-name>`, `<remote-as>`, `<remote-peer-ip>`, and `<policy-name>` with your specific values.
