Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure Nokia routers for VPN route exchange between different autonomous systems under BGP, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router
    bgp
        # Enable third-party next-hop for EBGP peers in the same subnet
        third-party-nexthop
        
        # Configure extended next-hop encoding for VPN routes
        extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
        
        # Disable delay on sending BGP withdrawals
        rapid-withdrawal
        
        # Configure best-path selection to treat EBGP and IBGP equally for VPN routes
        best-path-selection
            ebgp-ibgp-equal vpn-ipv4
        exit
        
        # Set up BGP group for inter-AS VPN peers
        group "INTER_AS_VPN"
            # Specify the remote peer's AS number
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            
            # Use local AS number if required (optional)
            local-as <local-as-number> private no-prepend-global-as
            
            # Advertise routes with local address as next-hop
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<remote-as-number>` with the actual remote AS number and `<local-as-number>` with your local AS number if needed. This configuration enables VPN route exchange while optimizing path selection and next-hop handling between different autonomous systems.
