Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP origin validation for both labeled IPv6 and unlabeled IPv4 routes from a specific peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family ipv4 ipv6 label-ipv6
            origin-validation
                ipv4
                    enable
                exit
                ipv6
                    enable
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

For enabling origin validation specifically for labeled IPv6 routes:
```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family label-ipv6
            origin-validation
                ipv6
                    enable
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

For enabling origin validation specifically for unlabeled IPv4 routes:
```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family ipv4
            origin-validation
                ipv4
                    enable
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```
