## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
enable-origin-validation [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ]
no enable-origin-validation
FuncDef:
When theenable-origin-validationcommand is added to the configuration of a group or neighbor, it causes every inbound IPv4 and/or IPv6 route from that peer to be marked with one of the 3 following origin validation states:
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4', 'Info': 'Enables origin validation processing for unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes.'}
{'Parameters': 'ipv6', 'Info': 'Enables origin validation processing for unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes.'}
{'Parameters': 'label-ipv4', 'Info': 'Enables origin validation processing for labeled IPv4 routes.'}
