To configure a Nokia router to drop a BGP peer immediately when its resolving route is removed, disable BGP graceful restart for the specific peer or group. Here’s the CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp 
    no graceful-restart
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp 
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            no graceful-restart
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This ensures the BGP session drops immediately when the resolving route is lost, bypassing the hold timer.
