To configure a Nokia router to drop a BGP peer immediately when its resolving route is removed, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        enable-peer-tracking
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This enables BGP peer tracking globally, causing the router to drop BGP peers immediately if their resolving route is removed, without waiting for the hold timer to expire. 

Optionally, you can also specify a peer-tracking policy if you need more granular control over which routes trigger the peer removal:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement "PEER-TRACK-POLICY"
            entry 10
                from
                    protocol direct
                exit
                action accept
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        enable-peer-tracking
        peer-tracking-policy "PEER-TRACK-POLICY"
        exit
    exit
exit
```
