## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to import all received VPN-IP routes into a dummy VRF for BGP next-hop resolution regardless of route targets, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        vpn-apply-import
        exit
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement ALLOW-ALL
            entry 10
                from
                    protocol bgp-vpn
                exit
                action accept
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    service
        vprn <dummy-vrf-service-id>
            bgp
                import ALLOW-ALL
            exit
        exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables applying base BGP import policies to VPN routes via `vpn-apply-import`
2. Creates a policy named `ALLOW-ALL` that accepts all BGP-VPN routes
3. Applies this policy to the dummy VRF's BGP instance

Replace `<dummy-vrf-service-id>` with your actual VPRN service ID for the dummy VRF.
