To ensure that all routes received from an EBGP peer have their most recent ASN in the AS_PATH attribute matching the configured peer AS of the session, use the `enforce-first-as` command at the appropriate BGP configuration level (global, group, or neighbor). Here are the CLI configuration commands:

At the global BGP level:
```
configure router bgp enforce-first-as
```

At the BGP group level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> enforce-first-as
```

At the BGP neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> enforce-first-as
```

Choose the appropriate level based on where you want to apply this enforcement. The command will verify that the last AS in the AS_PATH matches the configured peer AS for all received routes.
