To configure the Nokia router BGP to apply the route policies 'cust123-out' and 'backup-routes' for controlling outbound routes to specific peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            export "cust123-out backup-routes"
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of the specific peer you want to apply these policies to. The policies will control which routes are advertised to that peer.
