Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable BGP extended community filtering capability for outbound route filtering in a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name. This configuration enables the sending of link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes to EBGP peers in the specified group.

For neighbor-specific configuration (if needed):

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<ip-address>` with the specific neighbor IP address where you want to apply this filtering.
