## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise IPv6 multicast routes from a VPRN over the provider network using BGP, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
# Enter BGP configuration mode
configure router bgp

    # Enable rapid updates for multicast VPN IPv6 routes
    rapid-update mcast-vpn-ipv6

    # Configure the address family for multicast VPN IPv6
    family mcast-vpn-ipv6

    # Optionally, enable next-hop-self if needed for the BGP group or neighbor
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-self
    exit

    # Configure route targets for the VPRN if required
    route-target-list <comm-id>
exit

# Apply the configuration to the VPRN service
configure service vprn <vprn-id>
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            family mcast-vpn-ipv6
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<vprn-id>`, and `<comm-id>` with your specific values. This configuration enables BGP to advertise IPv6 multicast routes from the VPRN with the necessary address family and rapid update optimizations.
