Here are the CLI commands to configure next-hop-resolution options for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        policy <policy-name>
        use-bgp-routes
    exit
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
    exit
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send <send-limit> receive
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with your route policy name and `<send-limit>` with the desired path limit (1-16). 

For enabling extended next-hop encoding capability:
```
configure router bgp
    extended-nh-encoding
exit
```

To configure a primary IPv6 address for ORR (Optimal Route Reflection):
```
configure router bgp orr location <location-id>
    primary-ipv6-address <ipv6-address>
exit
```
