To configure a Nokia router to impose a local LLGR (Long-Lived Graceful Restart) stale time of 86400 seconds when receiving an LLGR capability from a BGP peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived-stale-time 86400
    exit
exit
```

This configuration sets the LLGR stale time to 86400 seconds globally for all BGP peers that advertise LLGR capability. The router will maintain stale routes for this duration during a graceful restart scenario.
