To configure BGP on a Nokia router to maintain the session permanently while rejecting any proposed hold-time below 120 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router
    bgp
        keepalive 40
        hold-time 120
exit all
```

The `hold-time 120` ensures the session will reject any proposed hold-time below 120 seconds. The `keepalive 40` sets the keepalive interval to one-third of the hold-time (as per BGP best practices), ensuring the session remains stable. These settings enforce a permanent BGP session with the specified timers.
