To configure BGP on a Nokia router with a hold time of 120 seconds and reject sessions proposing hold times below 60 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    timers 120 60
exit
```

The first value (120) sets the hold time in seconds, and the second value (60) sets the minimum acceptable hold time from peers. Any BGP session attempt with a proposed hold time below 60 seconds will be rejected.
