To enable load balancing for multiple IBGP paths with equal cost in your Nokia router's BGP configuration, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        ibgp-multipath
        exit
    exit
```

If you also want to include EBGP paths in the load balancing (EIBGP multipath), add these additional commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv4 ipv6
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

The first command (`ibgp-multipath`) enables IBGP multipath load balancing. The second set of commands (`ebgp-ibgp-equal`) allows EBGP and IBGP paths to be considered equally for load balancing across both IPv4 and IPv6 address families. Adjust the address family parameters (ipv4/ipv6) as needed for your specific requirements.
