Here are the CLI configuration commands to create the BGP inbound route policy with a secondary fallback policy:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement "CustomerX_Policy"
            entry 10
                action accept
                    local-preference 100
                exit
            exit
        commit
        policy-statement "LocalPref_100"
            entry 10
                action accept
                    local-preference 100
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        group "CustomerX_Group"
            neighbor <neighbor-IP>
                import "CustomerX_Policy" "LocalPref_100"
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Note: Replace `<neighbor-IP>` with the actual neighbor IP address. The configuration creates both policies and applies them to the specified neighbor, with "CustomerX_Policy" as primary and "LocalPref_100" as secondary fallback.
