Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 alternate paths per unlabeled IPv4 prefix while disabling the ability to receive multiple paths from BGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
    exit
configure router bgp add-paths
    ipv4 send 8 receive none
    exit
``` 

These commands enable the add-paths capability globally under BGP, then set the specific IPv4 unlabeled prefix behavior to send up to 8 paths while explicitly disabling the receive capability.
