To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 paths per unlabeled IPv6 unicast prefix while disabling the receive capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        multipath 8
        no enable-receive-ipv6
```

These commands:
1. Enable multipath support with a maximum of 8 paths under the BGP configuration context
2. Disable the receive capability for IPv6 prefixes

Note: The actual implementation may require additional configuration depending on your specific network setup and requirements.
