## Proposed answer:
To configure the Nokia router to declare a TCP connection down after missing 15 consecutive keepalives, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> hold-time 45
```

This sets the hold time to 45 seconds (assuming a default keepalive interval of 3 seconds, 15 missed keepalives × 3 = 45 seconds). The connection will be declared down if no keepalives are received within this period.

Note: You may need to adjust the `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` placeholders with your specific values. If the keepalive interval is different than 3 seconds, calculate the hold-time accordingly (hold-time = missed-keepalives × keepalive-interval).
