To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv6 paths per prefix while disabling the ability to receive multiple such routes, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
    exit
```

This configuration enables equal consideration of EBGP and IBGP routes for labeled-unicast IPv6, allowing up to 8 paths per prefix (assuming multipath is already configured). To disable receiving multiple labeled-unicast IPv6 routes, you would need to implement an import policy that rejects additional paths beyond the first one received for each prefix.
------------
