To configure a custom route preference (local-preference) of 150 for BGP labeled-unicast routes on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    local-preference 150
exit
```

This sets the BGP local-preference attribute to 150 globally for all BGP routes, including labeled-unicast routes. If you need to apply this specifically to a BGP group or neighbor, use these variations:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    local-preference 150
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    local-preference 150
exit
```
