To configure LDP tunneling for resolving next-hops of /32 IPv4 FECs and /128 IPv6 FECs on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        label-ipv4
            ldp
                tunnel-table-map
                    fec-type ipv4-prefix-length 32
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        label-ipv6
            ldp
                tunnel-table-map
                    fec-type ipv6-prefix-length 128
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables next-hop resolution under BGP
2. Configures LDP tunneling for both IPv4 (/32) and IPv6 (/128) FECs
3. Maps the specific prefix lengths to LDP tunnels

For proper operation, ensure:
- LDP is properly configured and operational on all relevant interfaces
- BGP is correctly configured to exchange labeled routes
- The necessary import/export policies are in place
------------
