To configure a Nokia router to attach a link-bandwidth extended community to BGP routes advertised to a specific EBGP neighbor, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
        neighbor <neighbor-ip-address>
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip-address>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This configuration will enable the attachment of link-bandwidth extended communities to IPv4 routes advertised to the specified EBGP neighbor.
