To attach a link-bandwidth extended community to BGP routes advertised to a specific EBGP peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> 
link-bandwidth send-to-ebgp ipv4
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the specific peer's IP address. This configuration will add the link-bandwidth extended community to IPv4 routes advertised to that EBGP peer.
