To configure the Nokia router to use the interface "core-link1" as the source IP address for BGP sessions within a specific group, follow these steps:

1. First, determine the IP address assigned to the "core-link1" interface.
2. Then, configure the BGP group to use this IP as the source address:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            local-address <ip-address-of-core-link1>
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name and `<ip-address-of-core-link1>` with the actual IP address of the "core-link1" interface.

If you need to create the BGP group first, use:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
```

Note: The `local-address` command is the standard way to specify the source IP for BGP sessions in Nokia routers, though it wasn't explicitly shown in the provided reference content. This is the correct approach for your requirement.
