Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure the local IP address as 192.168.100.10 for communication between a Nokia router and its BMP monitoring station, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
    bmp
        station <station-name>
            connection
                local-address 192.168.100.10
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<station-name>` with your BMP monitoring station's identifier. This will set the local IP address used for BMP communication to 192.168.100.10.
