Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure a BGP peer with virtual AS number 65535 while hiding both local and global AS numbers:

```
configure router bgp
    local-as 65535 private no-prepend-global-as
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            peer-as <remote-peer-as>
exit exit exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name, `<neighbor-ip>` with the peer's IP address, and `<remote-peer-as>` with the actual AS number of the remote BGP peer.

The `private` keyword hides the local AS in received paths, and `no-prepend-global-as` prevents prepending the global AS in advertised paths.
