To configure a Nokia router to discard routes containing your local AS number (65530) in the AS path while maintaining the BGP session, you'll need to create an outbound route policy that filters these routes. Here are the CLI commands:

```
# Enter BGP configuration mode
configure router bgp

# Create a route policy to reject routes containing AS 65530 in the path
policy-statement "REJECT_LOCAL_AS" 
    entry 10
        from as-path ".*65530.*"
        action reject
    exit
exit

# Apply the policy to inbound routes from the specific peer/group
group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
    neighbor "PEER_IP_ADDRESS"
        import "REJECT_LOCAL_AS"
    exit
exit
```

Alternatively, if you want to apply this to all peers:
```
group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
    import "REJECT_LOCAL_AS"
exit
```

Note: You'll need to replace "PEER_GROUP_NAME" and "PEER_IP_ADDRESS" with your actual peer group name and IP address. The AS path regular expression `".*65530.*"` will match any occurrence of your local AS (65530) anywhere in the AS path.
------------
