To handle BGP routes when detecting the local AS number (AS65530) in the AS path while maintaining the peer session, use the `loop-detect` command with the `ignore-loop` option:

```
configure router bgp
    loop-detect ignore-loop
exit
```

This configuration will ignore routes with loops in the AS path (including your local AS65530) but keep the BGP session active with the peer. The default behavior is already set to `ignore-loop`, so this command is only needed if it was previously changed to another option.
