This command enables the advertising of inactive BGP routes to other BGP peers. By default, BGP only advertises BGP routes to other BGP peers if a given BGP route is chosen by the route table manager as the most preferred route within the system and is active in the forwarding plane. This command allows system administrators to advertise a BGP route even though it is not the most preferred route within the system for a given destination.
匹配的cli
peer <ipv4-address> capability-advertise add-path { both | receive | send }
undo peer <ipv4-address> capability-advertise add-path { both | receive | send }
查询的def
The peer capability-advertise command enables optional BGP functions when a BGP peer advertises routes to its peer. The optional BGP functions include route-refresh, general router function, 4-byte AS number, and Add-Path.
The undo peer capability-advertise command restores the default setting.
By default, the route-refresh and 4-byte AS number functions are enabled, but the general router function and Add-Path are disabled.
