Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with a MED value of 5000 when MED is not already specified, you'll need to create and apply a route policy. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        prefix-list "all-prefixes"
            prefix 0.0.0.0/0 longer
        exit
        policy-statement "set-med-5000"
            entry 10
                from
                    prefix-list "all-prefixes"
                    med none
                exit
                action accept
                    med set 5000
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        export "set-med-5000"
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Creates a prefix-list matching all routes
2. Defines a policy that sets MED to 5000 for routes that don't have a MED value
3. Applies the policy as a BGP export policy

The policy will only modify routes that don't already have a MED value, leaving existing MED values unchanged.
