To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with a fixed MED value of 15000 when the MED is not explicitly set, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            always-compare-med infinity
```

This configuration ensures that routes without an explicit MED attribute will be treated as having a MED value of infinity (2³²-1), making them less preferred. However, if you specifically want to set a fixed MED value of 15000 for all advertised routes (regardless of whether they have a MED set or not), you would need to apply a policy to set the MED value. Here's an example:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement set-med
            entry 10
                action accept
                    med 15000
                exit
            exit
        commit
    bgp
        export "set-med"
```

This policy sets the MED to 15000 for all routes advertised via BGP. Apply this policy as an export policy under the BGP configuration.
