To configure a Nokia router to enforce a minimum interval of 45 seconds between BGP route advertisements to a specific peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            min-route-advertisement 45
            neighbor <peer-ip-address>
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of the specific peer. This sets the Minimum Route Advertisement Interval (MRAI) to 45 seconds for the specified peer.
