To configure Nokia routers to encode the type/subtype in advertised MVPN routes as 0x010b, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp mvpn-ipv4
```

This command enables the configuration of multicast VPN IPv4 routes, where you can set the type/subtype encoding as required. The specific encoding value (0x010b) would typically be part of the MVPN route attributes, though the exact syntax for setting this specific hex value may require additional context or parameters not shown in the provided reference content. 

For more precise control over MVPN route advertisements, you may also need to combine this with other MVPN-specific configurations under the BGP context.
