Here are the CLI commands to configure a BGP peer with IP address 192.0.2.15 on a Nokia router:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.15
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name and `<remote-as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the remote peer. 

Additional optional parameters you may want to configure include:
- `next-hop-self` - to use local address as next-hop
- `connect-retry <seconds>` - to set the BGP connect retry timer
- `local-as <as-number>` - to configure a local AS number
- `router-id <ip-address>` - to set the BGP router ID

For example, a more complete configuration might look like:
```
configure router bgp
    router-id <your-router-id>
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.15
            peer-as 65001
            next-hop-self
            connect-retry 60
exit all
```
