To add a BGP peer with IP address 192.168.10.5 on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.168.10.5
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<remote-as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the remote peer. 

If you need additional parameters like router-id, connect-retry, or local-as, you can include them within the same context. For example:

```
configure router bgp
    router-id <your-router-id>
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.168.10.5
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            connect-retry 30
```
