To adjust route resolution parameters for indirectly connected destinations in a Nokia router's BGP configuration, you need to enter the following contexts and commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-res
    use-bgp-routes
exit

configure router bgp next-hop-res labeled-routes
    transport-tunnel
    rr-use-route-table
exit
```

These commands enable:
1. Recursive next-hop resolution using BGP routes (`use-bgp-routes`)
2. Tunnel-based resolution for labeled routes (`transport-tunnel`)
3. Route table lookups for resolving next-hops when acting as a Route Reflector (`rr-use-route-table`)
