## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to preserve BGP next-hop information for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes when advertising to peers within the same group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to preserve BGP next-hop information for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes when advertising to peers within the same group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    no next-hop-self
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
exit
```

These commands:
1. Disable `next-hop-self` behavior at the BGP instance level (which would otherwise overwrite the next-hop)
2. Enable VPN route reflector forwarding to properly handle next-hop preservation for VPN routes

For more granular control at the group level, you could alternatively apply these settings to specific groups:

```
configure router bgp group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
    no next-hop-self
exit
```

This configuration ensures that BGP will preserve the original next-hop information when advertising routes to peers within the same group for both IPv4 and IPv6 address families.
